# Build context for the unibench target images.
#
# Reusing-unibench_build's target Dockerfiles run with this directory as their
# context -- that is why their COPY paths carry the Reusing-unibench_build/
# prefix. They need a handful of patches and data files out of it; everything
# else under there is experiment output, gigabytes of it.
#
# AFLplusplus_reusing and Reusing_scanner each build from their own directory
# as context (see tools/build.sh), so nothing here ever needs them.
AFLplusplus_reusing/
Reusing_scanner/

# LibAFL_reusing is the exception: the forkserver_libafl_reusing Dockerfiles COPY
# it out of this context rather than cloning it, so that a local edit lands in
# the image without a push and without docker serving a cached clone of an
# older commit. 12 MB of sources; its history and build output stay out.
LibAFL_reusing/.git/
LibAFL_reusing/**/target/

Reusing-unibench_build/
!Reusing-unibench_build/aflplusplus/
!Reusing-unibench_build/aflplusplus-cmplog/
!Reusing-unibench_build/aflplusplus-reusing-target/
!Reusing-unibench_build/aflplusplus-reusing_fuzzer_only/
!Reusing-unibench_build/reusing-scanner-target/
!Reusing-unibench_build/forkserver_libafl/
!Reusing-unibench_build/forkserver_libafl_reusing-target/
!Reusing-unibench_build/forkserver_libafl_reusing_fuzzer_only/
!Reusing-unibench_build/forkserver_storfuzz/
!Reusing-unibench_build/coverage/
!Reusing-unibench_build/ffmpeg/
!Reusing-unibench_build/tools/volume/seeds/

_build_cache/
target/
